{"title":"2010 IMO Shortlist Problems/G1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/G1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>(United Kingdom) Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> be an acute triangle with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> the feet of the altitudes lying on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/5/e657259c0995d2c36d46744bb4aa81471e6575ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> respectively. One of the intersection points of the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c128243ea8125d0bb007b8132dcfa44461df73a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and the circumcircle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. The lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/7/f874b39870586f0504f50a667f2bafedddf47904.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/3/c7387ef3aa3162cea3e516216d4ed946506bd30d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> meet at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" />. Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/0/da0acc3d5b6eb42db210a8b11d84482c9376c6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP = AQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/G1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2010_IMO_Shortlist_G1.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/6/65/2010_IMO_Shortlist_G1.png/400px-2010_IMO_Shortlist_G1.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"458\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/6/65/2010_IMO_Shortlist_G1.png/600px-2010_IMO_Shortlist_G1.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/6/65/2010_IMO_Shortlist_G1.png/800px-2010_IMO_Shortlist_G1.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure> \n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/a/68a601df1265456f5f689b9d7fa8c673bb8392be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\measuredangle$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> denote <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Directed_angles\" title=\"Directed angles\">directed angles</a> modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/0/3f0cd95f95238159d02dbcea0aca632c2928991c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"15\" />.\nAs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/2/5f2ed2fd8bf8df5be68457575894eabaebb8ab61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\measuredangle AFC =  \\measuredangle ADC = 90^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"187\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/4/7a44cbe0f1c0dcf92c7e963b5b0bc5139cc595d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AFDC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is cyclic.\n</p><p>As <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/2/4b27c19772130d03452c6ad72dc9fb2842d2f54c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$APBC$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/4/7a44cbe0f1c0dcf92c7e963b5b0bc5139cc595d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AFDC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> are both cyclic, \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/d/21df74560d23bc1d951b25c25c94ea4996b257d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\measuredangle QPA = \\measuredangle BPA = \\measuredangle BCA = \\measuredangle DCA = \\measuredangle DFA = \\measuredangle QFA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"457\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, we see <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/3/413f8a21ddff9e30653ec0aeda9e9330f4f8989a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AFPQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" /> is cyclic. Then\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/1/ca1120e5aadeb8199b79fe9a3261d7bde1072db2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\measuredangle AQP = \\measuredangle AFP = \\measuredangle AFE = \\measuredangle AHE = \\measuredangle DHE = \\measuredangle DCE = \\measuredangle BCA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"542\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>We deduce that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/8/658fd5fbf04935d0059bf15a4094525b17a24a77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\measuredangle AQP = \\measuredangle BCA = \\measuredangle QPA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"216\" height=\"18\" /> , which is enough to apply that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/8/6f826a09308897e7104cbf5e5a1b6d08b3c15db4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bigtriangleup APQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"57\" height=\"17\" /> is isosceles with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/0/da0acc3d5b6eb42db210a8b11d84482c9376c6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP = AQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>(Note that with directed angles in place, both the two possible configurations (shown in graph) are solved.)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/G1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_IMO_Shortlist_Problems\" title=\"2010 IMO Shortlist Problems\">2010 IMO Shortlist Problems</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//artofproblemsolving.com/community/c6h418633p2361970\">Discussion on AoPS</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017190246\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.019 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.046 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 135/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4670/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:30888:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017190246 and revision id 243120. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}